---
description: Use this skill to connect to the Linear API
alwaysApply: false
---
A LINEAR_API_KEY is required to use this skill. It is stored in the .env file.

### Verify authentication

```bash
set -a && source .env && set +a
uv run python -c "import json, os, urllib.request; q='query { viewer { id name } }'; req=urllib.request.Request('https://api.linear.app/graphql', data=json.dumps({'query': q}).encode(), headers={'Content-Type':'application/json','Authorization':os.environ['LINEAR_API_KEY']}); print(urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20).read().decode())"
```

### Manage a single blocking relation

- **Add (`A` blocks `B`)**: run `issueRelationCreate` with `type: blocks`, `issueId` = `A`, `relatedIssueId` = `B`.
- **Remove**: run `issueRelationDelete` with the relation `id`.

```bash
set -a && source .env && set +a
uv run python -c "import json, os, urllib.request; q='mutation{ issueRelationCreate(input:{type:blocks, issueId:\"ISSUE_A_ID\", relatedIssueId:\"ISSUE_B_ID\"}){ success issueRelation{ id } } }'; req=urllib.request.Request('https://api.linear.app/graphql', data=json.dumps({'query': q}).encode(), headers={'Content-Type':'application/json','Authorization':os.environ['LINEAR_API_KEY']}); print(urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20).read().decode())"
```

```bash
set -a && source .env && set +a
uv run python -c "import json, os, urllib.request; q='mutation{ issueRelationDelete(id:\"RELATION_ID\"){ success } }'; req=urllib.request.Request('https://api.linear.app/graphql', data=json.dumps({'query': q}).encode(), headers={'Content-Type':'application/json','Authorization':os.environ['LINEAR_API_KEY']}); print(urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20).read().decode())"
```